        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Requirements vary widely by city, county, and state, and often depend on whether the machine accepts cash at all, so this isn't something a general article can answer correctly for every reader. TODO: source not confirmed — check local amusement-device licensing and tax rules with your municipality before installing a cash-accepting machine."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is an arcade machine a good fit for a venue that only hosts events occasionally, like a banquet hall?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It depends on whether the venue runs the machine for cash payment or offers it as a free-play amenity bundled into event packages. A hall with infrequent, clustered bookings rarely generates enough cash drop across a full year to make coin-operated payback math work, so most occasional-event venues get more value treating it as part of the guest experience rather than as a revenue line. TODO: source not confirmed for typical event-venue coin-op drop rates, since no verified figures exist for this use case."
